    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Document any discrepancies and take photos to support the findings.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The recipient should compare the vehicle's odometer reading to the values mentioned in the LR billity (Load Delivery Receipt).</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If there is a discrepancy between the pickup and delivery odometer readings, document the difference and contact the sender.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the difference is within an acceptable margin (e.g., ±500 km for vehicles with a regular mileage), proceed with the delivery. If the difference is significant, refer to the sender for clarification.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The recipient should sign the condition sign-off document provided by the sender, acknowledging their acceptance of the vehicle's condition and verifying that the vehicle is in the same condition as when it was picked up.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>For your records, make sure to take a photo of the recipient signing the condition sign-off document.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Once the recipient signs the document, provide a copy to the recipient and keep the original for your records.</span></li>
	</ul>
	<p>By performing a thorough inspection, verifying the odometer reading, and obtaining a signed condition sign-off, you can ensure a smooth delivery process and maintain transparency with both the sender and recipient.</p>
	<p>In case of any further clarification or disputes, referring to the pickup photos, the LR billity, and the condition sign-off document will serve as valuable evidence.</p>
	<p>By following these steps, you can confidently hand over the vehicle and maintain a well-documented history of the transportation process.</p>
	<p>It is essential to perform these checks during daylight hours to ensure accurate evaluation of the vehicle's condition.</p>
